invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: diff_p256_wide
reason: the incomplete Jacobian addition adds s1 * hhh to Y3 where the
  formula takes it away, so Y3 comes out for another point.
  bin/diff_p256_wide holds the steps to spec/lean/Spec/P256WidePoint.lean's
  addJacobianIncomplete, coordinate for coordinate, which is what makes
  the Lean proof that the steps add two points a proof about this file.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&t, &s1, &hhh);
    p256_wide_fe_sub(&y3, &y3, &t);
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&t, &s1, &hhh);
    p256_wide_fe_add(&y3, &y3, &t);
